    "wikipedia_summary": "<i><b>Dianthus hyssopifolius</b></i>, the <b>fringed pink</b> (a name it shares with <i>Dianthus superbus</i>), is a species of flowering plant in the family Caryophyllaceae. It is native to Portugal, Spain, and France, and it has been introduced to Great Britain. A subshrub, it is available from commercial suppliers.",
